        "rationale": "SimiC consumes a valid order between states that SPATHI does not use. Both are evaluated only where the simulator emits an ordered-state contract, separately from the information-matched primary ranking.",
        "statistical_role": "separate_family_analysis",
        "route_ids": ["spathi", "simic-ordered"]
      },
      {
        "id": "c-lineage-aware",
        "label": "C · Lineage-aware directed inference",
        "rationale": "Joint scMTNI consumes a simulator-derived lineage topology that SPATHI does not use. It is evaluated with SPATHI only on datasets whose lineage is part of the valid generation contract, and never pooled with the primary ranking.",
        "statistical_role": "separate_family_analysis",
        "route_ids": ["spathi", "scmtni-lineage"]
      },
      {
        "id": "d-directed-all-gene",
        "label": "D · Directed unrestricted-regulator fitting",
        "rationale": "MetaSEM and kScReNI fit without a transcription-factor restriction, whereas SPATHI uses the declared TF list. Every output is nevertheless scored on the same TF-to-target candidate space. The unequal fitting search space makes this a separate secondary analysis rather than part of the information-matched primary ranking.",
        "statistical_role": "separate_family_analysis",
        "route_ids": ["spathi", "metasem", "kscreni"]
      },
      {
        "id": "e-undirected-topology",
        "label": "E · Undirected topology recovery",
        "rationale": "Direction cannot be compared fairly for these estimators. Their outputs and the direction-collapsed SPATHI network are scored on the same TF-to-target candidate space only as undirected topology, separately from every directed family.",
        "statistical_role": "separate_family_analysis",
        "route_ids": ["spathi", "pidc", "clr", "ppcor", "aracne3", "cespgrn", "lioness"]
      }
